cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use farr-browser, please cite it as below."
title: "farr-browser: a polite browser for AI agents"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Sharifi
    given-names: Kiomars
keywords:
  - browser automation
  - AI agents
  - Model Context Protocol
  - robots.txt
abstract: >-
  A browser for AI agents that keeps a page open between calls. The agent sees
  one line per actionable element, each with a ref, acts on refs, and is told
  what measurably changed. Stale refs are refused, controls that buy, pay,
  delete or send are refused unless explicitly allowed, confirm() dialogs are
  dismissed by default, robots.txt is honoured and requests are paced per site.
  It also reads pages as markdown, downloads files, runs declarative site
  skills, uses proxies the user brings, and serves all of this over MCP.
